From: Zurker <91011862+hershate@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 05:00:14 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Papo: batch 166 - release pathfinder stale-node retention

BinaryHeap.clear() only reset size, so each mob's PathFinder pinned its
last search's unpopped frontier plus every historically grown-but-never-
popped slot between searches (entity soak census: 26,683 Nodes / 1.71MB
+ 2,031 Node[] arrays / 500KB across ~679 mobs, ~3.2KB per mob, scaling
with mob count and search length). The array beyond size is never read
by the search logic; getHeap() hands debug consumers a dense
Arrays.copyOf(heap, size) snapshot, so nulling is unobservable there.
The 32-slot neighbor scratch gets the same treatment after each search
(slots rewritten bounded by the returned count before every read).

Zero behavioral difference; pure release-after-last-reader.

diff --git a/net/minecraft/world/level/pathfinder/BinaryHeap.java b/net/minecraft/world/level/pathfinder/BinaryHeap.java
index b867357561672b53daa0294f32545da617c19fda..eff1184ca09f8c93de75da999922409e74c15589 100644
--- a/net/minecraft/world/level/pathfinder/BinaryHeap.java
+++ b/net/minecraft/world/level/pathfinder/BinaryHeap.java
@@ -24,6 +24,14 @@ public class BinaryHeap {
     }
 
     public void clear() {
+        // Papo start - batch 166 (R25): the heap array kept references to the search's
+        // residue (unpopped frontier nodes and historically grown-but-never-popped slots)
+        // alive between searches - measured 26,683 stale Nodes / 1.71MB + grown Node[]
+        // arrays across ~679 mobs in the entity soak, pinned solely by these slots. The
+        // array beyond `size` is never read by the search logic, and debug consumers get
+        // an Arrays.copyOf(heap, size) snapshot from getHeap(), so nulling is unobservable.
+        Arrays.fill(this.heap, null);
+        // Papo end - batch 166 (R25)
         this.size = 0;
     }
 
diff --git a/net/minecraft/world/level/pathfinder/PathFinder.java b/net/minecraft/world/level/pathfinder/PathFinder.java
index 168b475b38b2872b27c1ab15f6846323ac16dd2c..c863251c14ac2b86e4984e85c72320f78585f0ea 100644
--- a/net/minecraft/world/level/pathfinder/PathFinder.java
+++ b/net/minecraft/world/level/pathfinder/PathFinder.java
@@ -55,6 +55,12 @@ public class PathFinder {
             // Paper end - Perf: remove streams and optimize collection
             Path path = this.findPath(start, map, maxRange, reachRange, maxVisitedNodesMultiplier);
             this.nodeEvaluator.done();
+            // Papo start - batch 166 (R25): same stale-retention family as the heap clear -
+            // the 32-slot neighbor scratch kept the last getNeighbors() results alive after
+            // the search ended. Slots are fully rewritten (bounded by the returned count)
+            // before every read, so nulling between searches is unobservable.
+            java.util.Arrays.fill(this.neighbors, null);
+            // Papo end - batch 166 (R25)
             return path;
         }
     }
